98 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (Expansion plans often follow population size and overlook how much people can spend and how fast costs are rising. A large market with weak purchasing power or rising prices can still leave thin margins. This project turns regional statistics into a dashboard that shows where wages are strong, where price pressure is low, and where risk is building.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
99 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (The dashboard combines provincial price index \(CPI\), minimum wage, and population data for 2024 and 2025. In Power Query, I standardized data types and created a month index column used with Sort by Column so trends run from January to December. The model follows a star schema with a fact table and a province dimension, and DAX measures such as Avg_Inflation and Market_Score feed three pages: Executive Summary, Market Size & Income, and Inflation & Cost Risks.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
